A||N||4||Fie Ro||Engine running.........bad||||1||
Z||000000||Fie Ro||12-29-2001||10:29 AM||||I finally have got my engine running. see topic:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014454.html]http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014454.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014454.html]http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014454.html</A>  <P>But it seems 1 or 2 cilinders aren't running, when I pull the sparkplugwire of those cilinders there's no change...<BR>-Injectors are rebuilt<BR>-new sparkplugs (getting spark). checked with timing light.<BR>-no bad smell from exhaust (no unburned fuel)<BR>-code 44 lean exhaust!<BR>-timing checked and reset (in diagnostic mode!)<P>I think 2 injectors are not firing, connections seem ok. Strange new thing is that according to the voltmeter the battery isn't charging. getting about 10/11 volts...could that affect  the injectors?<BR>battery is 2 years old, alternator 1 year...<P>I hope to get some advice, don't want to take the plenum off again ;(<P>Roderick<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://homepage.mac.com/rewq/images/signature.jpg">     <P>[URL=http://homepage.mac.com/rewq/html/fiero.html[/URL] <P>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200<p>[This message has been edited by Fie Ro (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||12-29-2001||06:02 PM||||You could get a long piece of hose and use it like a stetoscope to listen to the injectors, use a suitable diameter hose. When they are working you should hear them clicking. If you hear no sound they are not actuating.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||12-29-2001||06:07 PM||||Guess I would begin by checking the 2 fuel injection fuses in the fusebox under dash.  If one fuse is blown (open), I think only half (three) injectors will be operating.  Sorry if you have already been down this path, but it's all I can think of for now.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTDude||12-30-2001||09:58 AM||||use a noid light......purchased at local parts store....hook it up to the 2 wires going to the injector and see if they flash when engine is turned over or started.  If not.....and not the fuses....it's the computer driver circuit most likely and you will need to replace puter. Check all fuses...this can cause alt. not to charge.  I'd work on fixing the alt. prob. first cause the computer depends on very minute voltages to do it's job.  Hope this helps.<P>Phil Pettus<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a_7.JPG">  <P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT<p>[This message has been edited by GTDude (edited 12-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnF||12-30-2001||01:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fie Ro:<BR><B>isn't charging. getting about 10/11 volts...could that affect  the injectors?<P>I hope to get some advice, don't want to take the plenum off again ;(<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Low voltage output can affect many things.  Until you get the full voltage output(probably alternator - see what it is putting out!  The 10V to 11V is FAR below the required 13.5+), don't bother checking anything else.<P>After that is fixed, get back on the forum if you still have a problem.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://photo.msn.s8.com/MS8zLzAvMS8xMDg3LzE1NS8zMi9INU54UkJyRnlPbnZkaDdvRENhLW13/2a787ccc86b5da461605f26eef23ff8a/clbk=0h9xCkj4Yyo6VbTdcNrmhglJSkAWB6C91volMeDlp0h*oii8TPGa20kyOxpdcqzP8qgFSFmsURSXXLzrLUqyll5ofimdP92*FNFuzBBDM1PEajQxQ*Q8WWq*rfvz6!x4pUtE2EsH24ClDyP3oWXL*C!sOjXA63RMH7rLXNlHSu0Yga0L9A7awE0Vo4vjfHksI0c5clA2zMM!vGsSGqWEfH6rUngsCm7dmRIGCL4B98JxdRCo19jb2zHG1Q2F8!3f0GHxu0h66objRD*CveMNtxaf03Gv9Wi1/jpg.jpg">   <P>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||12
